{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e87b4112-f8c7-430e-a56c-6fe0ff814c2b",
    "name": "ZeroWall - Zero-Trust API Gateway",
    "description": "Postman collection for the ZeroWall demo. Mirrors the 10 scenarios in scripts/test_attacks.sh.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this collection AND the ZeroWall environment file.\n2. Select the 'ZeroWall - Dev' environment from the dropdown.\n3. Promote user2 to admin once via AWS CLI:\n   `aws cognito-idp admin-update-user-attributes --user-pool-id us-east-2_ZEaM80bI4 --username desairaj1807@gmail.com --user-attributes Name=custom:role,Value=admin --region us-east-2`\n\n## Run order (manual)\nAuth \u2192 S02 (User), Auth \u2192 S02b (Admin), then any scenario.\n\n## Run order (Collection Runner)\nRun the entire collection. Folders execute in this order: Auth, Notes CRUD, RBAC, Attacks, Rate Limiting.\nNote: the Rate Limiting folder request should be excluded from a normal collection run (it depletes the user's window). Run it separately with iterations=150.\n\n## Scenario index\nS01 Signup, S02 Login, S03 Create note, S04 No token, S05 Expired token, S06 DELETE as user, S07 DELETE as admin, S08 Tampered token, S09 Replay, S10 Rate limit.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "S01 - Sign up",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/signup",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "signup"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Registers a new user. Reusing an existing email returns a user-exists error, which still proves the endpoint is reachable."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sign up may return 200/201 (new) or 409/400 (already exists). Both prove the endpoint is reachable.",
                  "pm.test('Endpoint reachable', () => {",
                  "    const ok = [200, 201].includes(pm.response.code);",
                  "    const userExists = [400, 409].includes(pm.response.code) && /exist/i.test(pm.response.text());",
                  "    pm.expect(ok || userExists).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S02 - Login (User)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Logs in the regular user. The test script saves the returned idToken to the userToken env var for subsequent requests."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = json.idToken || (json.data && json.data.idToken);",
                  "pm.test('idToken returned', () => pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "if (token) { pm.environment.set('userToken', token); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S02b - Login (Admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Logs in the admin user. Assumes user2 has been promoted to custom:role=admin via the AWS CLI before running this request."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = json.idToken || (json.data && json.data.idToken);",
                  "pm.test('idToken returned', () => pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "if (token) { pm.environment.set('adminToken', token); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Cognito-backed signup and login. Login requests automatically save tokens to env vars."
    },
    {
      "name": "Notes CRUD",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "S03 - Create note (valid token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"Postman test note\", \"content\": \"Created via Postman S03\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Creates a note as the regular user. Saves the returned noteId for use in later scenarios."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const noteId = (json.data && json.data.noteId) || json.noteId;",
                  "pm.test('noteId returned', () => pm.expect(noteId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "if (noteId) { pm.environment.set('userNoteId', noteId); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List notes (GET /notes)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "description": "Lists all notes for the authenticated user."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get note by id (GET /notes/{id})",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes/{{userNoteId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes", "{{userNoteId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Retrieves the note created in S03."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update note (PUT /notes/{id})",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes/{{userNoteId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes", "{{userNoteId}}"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"Updated title\", \"content\": \"Updated content\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Updates the note from S03."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Standard CRUD operations against /notes. All require the userToken env var to be set (run Auth \u2192 S02 first)."
    },
    {
      "name": "RBAC",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Setup - Create admin note",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"Admin note for S07\", \"content\": \"To be deleted by S07\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Creates a note as admin so S07 has something to delete. Run before S07. Requires adminToken (Auth \u2192 S02b first)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const noteId = (json.data && json.data.noteId) || json.noteId;",
                  "if (noteId) { pm.environment.set('adminNoteId', noteId); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S06 - DELETE as user (expect 403)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes/{{userNoteId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes", "{{userNoteId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Regular user attempts DELETE. RBAC should reject with 403 (user role does not have DELETE permission)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 403', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(403));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S07 - DELETE as admin (expect 200)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes/{{adminNoteId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes", "{{adminNoteId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Admin deletes their own note. Note: data isolation means admin can only DELETE notes they own (userId is always the authorizer-supplied partition key)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 or 204', () => pm.expect([200, 204]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Role-based access control. user role can read/write own notes but cannot DELETE; admin can DELETE."
    },
    {
      "name": "Attacks",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "S04 - Create note WITHOUT token (expect 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"should fail\", \"content\": \"no auth\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Sends POST /notes with no Authorization header. API Gateway rejects with 401 before reaching the authorizer."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S05 - Expired token (expect 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{expiredToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"should fail\", \"content\": \"expired\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Requires the expiredToken env var to be set. Capture one via `./scripts/test_attacks.sh --prep-expired` and wait 65+ minutes for it to expire, then paste into the env var."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const expired = pm.environment.get('expiredToken');",
                  "if (!expired) {",
                  "    console.warn('\u26a0\ufe0f  S05 skipped: set the expiredToken env var (capture one via test_attacks.sh --prep-expired and wait 65+ min).');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const expired = pm.environment.get('expiredToken');",
                  "if (!expired) {",
                  "    pm.test('SKIPPED - no expiredToken env var set', () => true);",
                  "} else {",
                  "    pm.test('Status is 401', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(401));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S08 - Tampered token (expect 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{tamperedToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"should fail\", \"content\": \"tampered\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Pre-request script takes userToken and replaces the last character with X. The authorizer should reject the tampered token via signature verification failure."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const userToken = pm.environment.get('userToken');",
                  "if (!userToken) {",
                  "    throw new Error('userToken not set. Run Auth \u2192 S02 - Login (User) first.');",
                  "}",
                  "// Match the bash test exactly: replace the last character with X",
                  "const tampered = userToken.slice(0, -1) + 'X';",
                  "pm.environment.set('tamperedToken', tampered);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "S09 - Replay (reuse valid token, expect 201)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"title\": \"replay\", \"content\": \"valid token reused\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Reuses a valid token. Both calls succeed - this proves token expiry IS the protection against replay, not a one-time-use mechanism. Run twice (or iterations=2 in Runner)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(201));",
                  "// Run this request twice in a row (or via Runner with iterations=2). Both calls",
                  "// should succeed - this proves token expiry is the only protection against replay,",
                  "// not a one-time-use mechanism."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Adversarial scenarios. Each verifies a specific security guarantee."
    },
    {
      "name": "Rate Limiting",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "S10 - Rate limit GET /notes (run via Runner, iterations=150)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notes"]
            },
            "description": "To reproduce the rate-limit demo:\n1. Open Collection Runner\n2. Select only this request\n3. Set Iterations: 150, Delay: 0\n4. Run\n\nExpected: ~99 requests return 200, then ~50 return 429 starting around iteration 100. If you re-run within the same minute window, you'll see 429s immediately - wait 60s for the window to reset."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Run via Collection Runner with iterations=150 to reproduce the rate-limit demo.",
                  "// Expected: ~99 requests return 200, then ~50 return 429 starting around #100.",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 or 429', () => pm.expect([200, 429]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 429) {",
                  "    pm.test('Has rate-limit body', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('RATE_LIMITED'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Per-user, per-minute rate limiting (default 100/min, configurable via RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE on zerowall-notes-handler)."
    }
  ]
}
